      ******************************************************************
      *  Testsuite : COCRDLIC CARD LIST BROWSE TRANSACTION
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/COCRDLIC.cbl
      *
      *  COCRDLIC is the credit-card list browse CICS transaction.
      *  RECEIVEs optional account-id/card-number filters, validates
      *  via 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT and 2220-EDIT-CARD, enters the
      *  canonical CICS browse pattern (STARTBR/READNEXT/ENDBR),
      *  PF8 forward via 9000-READ-FORWARD, PF7 back via 9100-READ-
      *  BACKWARDS, 9500-FILTER-RECORDS gates row admission.
      *
      *  External dependency mocked: CALL 'DFHEI1' (CICS API stand-in
      *  used by CICS translator).  Internal paragraphs are NEVER
      *  mocked; structural conventions inherit from the canonical
      *  exemplar tests/cobol-check/COSGN00C.cut.
      *
      *  Test categories (7 testcases)
      *  -----------------------------
      *    TC1 - 2220-EDIT-CARD accepts valid 16-digit card (L1036)
      *    TC2 - YYYY-STORE-PFKEY DFHPF8 -> CCARD-AID-PFK08
      *    TC3 - YYYY-STORE-PFKEY DFHPF7 -> CCARD-AID-PFK07
      *    TC4 - 1400-SETUP-MESSAGE EOF advisory (L905-909)
      *    TC5 - 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT rejects non-numeric (L1017)
      *    TC6 - YYYY-STORE-PFKEY DFHPF3 -> CCARD-AID-PFK03
      *    TC7 - 9500-FILTER-RECORDS excludes account mismatch
      *
      *  Test user: USER0001 per AAP 0.10.2; upstream COMEN01C/CM00.
      *  Off-platform deferral: CICS-translator-dependent EVALUATE
      *  WS-RESP-CD pathways require MOCK CICS support (cobol-check
      *  > 0.2.16) for end-to-end PERFORM coverage.
      *
      *  References
      *  ----------
      *    AAP 0.5.1, 0.7.1, 0.10.1, 0.10.2
      *    app/cbl/COCRDLIC.cbl / app/cpy/CSSTRPFY.cpy
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy / DFHEI1.cbl
      *    tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/CARD-FIXTURE-001.cpy
      *
      *  DFHEI1 fail-loudly safety net (QA CP4 Phase 5.2): the
      *  COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG anchor below is dropped silently by
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16; runner-script Step 5 injects the
      *  EXTERNAL field declarations into merged WS, and BEFORE-
      *  EACH resets WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED for per-testcase
      *  isolation of the safety-net flag.
      ******************************************************************
       COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.

       TESTSUITE 'COCRDLIC CARD LIST BROWSE TRANSACTION'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset.  Clears all WS
      *  groups COCRDLIC reads/writes (MISC-STORAGE, CC-WORK-AREAS,
      *  COMMAREA, PROGCOMMAREA, SCREEN-DATA, CARD-RECORD, CCRDLIAI,
      *  DATE-TIME, COMMAREA buffer), resets RETURN-CODE and the
      *  WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED safety-net flag, then seeds the
      *  COMMAREA with USER0001 (per AAP 0.10.2) and FROM-PROGRAM
      *  COMEN01C/CM00 to reflect the upstream caller.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE WS-MISC-STORAGE
            INITIALIZE CC-WORK-AREAS
            INITIALIZE CARDDEMO-COMMAREA
            INITIALIZE WS-THIS-PROGCOMMAREA
            INITIALIZE WS-SCREEN-DATA
            INITIALIZE CARD-RECORD
            INITIALIZE CCRDLIAI
            INITIALIZE WS-DATE-TIME
            MOVE SPACES     TO WS-COMMAREA
            MOVE ZERO       TO RETURN-CODE
            MOVE 'N'        TO WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED
            MOVE 'USER0001' TO CDEMO-USER-ID
            MOVE 'U'        TO CDEMO-USER-TYPE
            MOVE 'COMEN01C' TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM
            MOVE 'CM00'     TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID
       END-BEFORE.


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- 2220-EDIT-CARD accepts a valid 16-digit card number
      *
      *  Drives 2220-EDIT-CARD (production lines 1036-1067) along
      *  the SUCCESS path that gates 9000-READ-FORWARD downstream.
      *  The paragraph executes:
      *
      *    SET FLG-CARDFILTER-BLANK TO TRUE                (line 1039)
      *    IF CC-CARD-NUM = LOW-VALUES OR SPACES OR
      *       CC-CARD-NUM-N EQUAL ZEROS                    (line 1042-4)
      *        ... (FALSE; '0500024453765740' is non-zero)
      *    IF CC-CARD-NUM IS NOT NUMERIC                   (line 1052)
      *        ... (FALSE; '0500024453765740' is all-numeric)
      *    ELSE                                            (line 1063)
      *        MOVE CC-CARD-NUM-N TO CDEMO-CARD-NUM        (line 1064)
      *        SET FLG-CARDFILTER-ISVALID TO TRUE          (line 1065)
      *    END-IF.
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC1 prelude: production
      *  invariant is that 9000-READ-FORWARD's STARTBR (line 1129)
      *  only runs when both 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT and 2220-EDIT-CARD
      *  validate their respective filter inputs (the line-431-435
      *  IF guard requires NOT FLG-ACCTFILTER-NOT-OK AND NOT FLG-
      *  CARDFILTER-NOT-OK).  A regression that broadened the IS
      *  NOT NUMERIC clause would surface here as a failed FLG-
      *  CARDFILTER-ISVALID assertion.
      *
      *  Why '0500024453765740' is the chosen valid input
      *  ------------------------------------------------
      *  CARD-NUM byte-extracted from app/data/ASCII/carddata.txt
      *  record 1 via CARD-FIXTURE-001 (per the schema dependency).
      *  Using a fixture-sourced card number rather than a synthetic
      *  literal keeps the testsuite traceable to its production
      *  seed data per AAP Section 0.4.4.  16 chars (matches CC-
      *  CARD-NUM PIC X(16)), all-numeric, non-zero.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '1'         - WS-EDIT-CARD-FLAG flipped by SET FLG-
      *                  CARDFILTER-ISVALID (line 1065; 88-level
      *                  VALUE '1' per COCRDLIC.cbl line 67).
      *    0500024453765740
      *                - CDEMO-CARD-NUM populated by line 1064 MOVE
      *                  CC-CARD-NUM-N TO CDEMO-CARD-NUM (PIC 9(16)
      *                  per COCOM01Y line 41).
      *    SPACES      - WS-ERROR-MSG retains BEFORE-EACH default
      *                  (88-level WS-ERROR-MSG-OFF on VALUE SPACES
      *                  per line 118).  No diagnostic on success.
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES asserts the production
      *  invariant that 2220-EDIT-CARD contains zero EXEC CICS
      *  verbs.  Same pattern as COCRDSLC TC1 / COTRN00C TC2 --
      *  pure-WS validation paragraphs.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDLIC 2220-EDIT-CARD accepts valid 16-digit num'
            MOVE '0500024453765740' TO CC-CARD-NUM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 2220-EDIT-CARD THRU 2220-EDIT-CARD-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-CARD-FLAG TO BE '1'
            EXPECT CDEMO-CARD-NUM TO BE 0500024453765740
            EXPECT WS-ERROR-MSG TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- YYYY-STORE-PFKEY maps DFHPF8 to CCARD-AID-PFK08
      *
      *  Drives YYYY-STORE-PFKEY (CSSTRPFY copybook lines 17-79,
      *  COPY-included into COCRDLIC's PROCEDURE DIVISION at line
      *  1416).  This paragraph is the dispatch table 0000-MAIN
      *  performs at line 349-350 BEFORE entering the EVALUATE TRUE
      *  block at line 418.  It maps the EIBAID byte to a 5-char
      *  keyword stored in CCARD-AID; downstream code tests CCARD-
      *  AID via the 88-level conditions in CVCRD01Y lines 4-19.
      *
      *  TC2 tests the PF8 forward-paging arm:
      *
      *    WHEN EIBAID IS EQUAL TO DFHPF8                   (line 44)
      *      SET CCARD-AID-PFK08 TO TRUE                    (line 45)
      *
      *  CCARD-AID-PFK08 is the 88-level VALUE 'PFK08' on CCARD-AID
      *  (CVCRD01Y line 21); the SET TO TRUE writes 'PFK08' into
      *  the parent group field.
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC2 "PF8 forward page
      *  READNEXT continues".  The literal AAP TC2 requires driving
      *  0000-MAIN's WHEN CCARD-AID-PFK08 AND CA-NEXT-PAGE-EXISTS
      *  branch (lines 486-497) end-to-end through 9000-READ-
      *  FORWARD's STARTBR + READNEXT loop -- both require the
      *  CICS translator pass.  TC2 substitutes a direct PERFORM of
      *  YYYY-STORE-PFKEY with EIBAID=DFHPF8 to validate the FIRST
      *  mapping in the dispatch chain that reaches the WHEN
      *  CCARD-AID-PFK08 branch.
      *
      *  Differential vs TC3 / TC6: TC3 tests DFHPF7 -> 'PFK07',
      *  TC6 tests DFHPF3 -> 'PFK03'; the three together prove the
      *  PFKey arms route to distinct 88-level VALUEs and cannot
      *  be conflated.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'PFK08'    - CCARD-AID populated by SET CCARD-AID-PFK08
      *                 TO TRUE (CSSTRPFY line 45).  88-level VALUE
      *                 declared on CVCRD01Y line 21.
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES -- pure dispatch paragraph.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDLIC YYYY-STORE-PFKEY maps DFHPF8 to PFK08'
            MOVE DFHPF8 TO EIBAID
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM YYYY-STORE-PFKEY THRU YYYY-STORE-PFKEY-EXIT
            EXPECT CCARD-AID TO BE 'PFK08'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- YYYY-STORE-PFKEY maps DFHPF7 to CCARD-AID-PFK07
      *
      *  Drives YYYY-STORE-PFKEY (CSSTRPFY) along the PF7 backward-
      *  paging arm:
      *
      *    WHEN EIBAID IS EQUAL TO DFHPF7                   (line 42)
      *      SET CCARD-AID-PFK07 TO TRUE                    (line 43)
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC3 "PF7 backward page
      *  READPREV navigates back".  The literal AAP TC3 requires
      *  driving 0000-MAIN's WHEN CCARD-AID-PFK07 AND NOT CA-FIRST
      *  -PAGE branch (lines 501-513) end-to-end through 9100-
      *  READ-BACKWARDS' STARTBR + READPREV loop -- both require
      *  the CICS translator pass.
      *
      *  Differential vs TC2: a regression that swaps the PF7 / PF8
      *  arms of the EVALUATE would be detected by TC3 failing
      *  (CCARD-AID would become 'PFK08') while TC2 still passed.
      *  Hence both arms are required for differential coverage.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'PFK07'    - CCARD-AID populated by SET CCARD-AID-PFK07
      *                 TO TRUE (CSSTRPFY line 43).  88-level VALUE
      *                 declared on CVCRD01Y line 20.
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES -- no-CICS invariant.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDLIC YYYY-STORE-PFKEY maps DFHPF7 to PFK07'
            MOVE DFHPF7 TO EIBAID
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM YYYY-STORE-PFKEY THRU YYYY-STORE-PFKEY-EXIT
            EXPECT CCARD-AID TO BE 'PFK07'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- 1400-SETUP-MESSAGE PF8-at-end emits 'NO MORE PAGES'
      *
      *  Drives 1400-SETUP-MESSAGE (production lines 895-932) along
      *  the PF8-at-end advisory branch (lines 905-909):
      *
      *    WHEN CCARD-AID-PFK08                             (line 905)
      *     AND CA-NEXT-PAGE-NOT-EXISTS                     (line 906)
      *     AND CA-LAST-PAGE-SHOWN                          (line 907)
      *      MOVE 'NO MORE PAGES TO DISPLAY'                (line 908)
      *      TO WS-ERROR-MSG                                (line 909)
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC4 "End-of-file (READNEXT
      *  EIBRESP=20 ENDFILE) handled gracefully": when 9000-READ-
      *  FORWARD's READNEXT (line 1146) returns DFHRESP(ENDFILE)
      *  at line 1233, production sets CA-NEXT-PAGE-NOT-EXISTS at
      *  line 1235; on the NEXT PF8 press, 1400-SETUP-MESSAGE sees
      *  both CA-NEXT-PAGE-NOT-EXISTS and CA-LAST-PAGE-SHOWN TRUE
      *  and emits the user advisory.  The branch encodes the
      *  invariant that a forward-page request after the last page
      *  has already been shown surfaces a user-visible advisory
      *  rather than issuing a doomed STARTBR / READNEXT.
      *
      *  88-level conditional names exercised:
      *    CCARD-AID-PFK08         CVCRD01Y line 21 VALUE 'PFK08';
      *                            set TRUE via TC4 prelude MOVE.
      *    CA-NEXT-PAGE-NOT-EXISTS COCRDLIC.cbl line 243 VALUE
      *                            LOW-VALUES; set TRUE via MOVE.
      *    CA-LAST-PAGE-SHOWN      COCRDLIC.cbl line 240 VALUE 0;
      *                            explicitly MOVE 0 for documented
      *                            intent.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'NO MORE PAGES TO DISPLAY' - WS-ERROR-MSG literal MOVE'd
      *               verbatim by production line 908; ERRMSGO OF
      *               CCRDLIAO populated by line 924 MOVE WS-ERROR-
      *               MSG TO ERRMSGO.  Asserting BOTH source and
      *               target proves the MOVE chain is intact.
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES asserts that 1400-SETUP-
      *  MESSAGE contains zero EXEC CICS verbs (1500-SEND-SCREEN
      *  is a separate paragraph).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDLIC 1400-SETUP-MESSAGE PF8-at-end advisory'
            MOVE 'PFK08'    TO CCARD-AID
            MOVE LOW-VALUES TO WS-CA-NEXT-PAGE-IND
            MOVE 0          TO WS-CA-LAST-PAGE-DISPLAYED
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 1400-SETUP-MESSAGE THRU 1400-SETUP-MESSAGE-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-ERROR-MSG TO BE 'NO MORE PAGES TO DISPLAY'
            EXPECT ERRMSGO OF CCRDLIAO TO BE 'NO MORE PAGES TO DISPLAY'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT rejects non-numeric account id
      *
      *  Drives 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT (production lines 1003-1030) along
      *  the IS NOT NUMERIC rejection path -- the format-fail gate
      *  that prevents 9000-READ-FORWARD's STARTBR from being
      *  invoked on a malformed filter input.  The relevant branch:
      *
      *    IF CC-ACCT-ID IS NOT NUMERIC                    (line 1017)
      *        SET INPUT-ERROR TO TRUE                     (line 1018)
      *        SET FLG-ACCTFILTER-NOT-OK TO TRUE           (line 1019)
      *        SET FLG-PROTECT-SELECT-ROWS-YES TO TRUE     (line 1020)
      *        MOVE 'ACCOUNT FILTER,IF SUPPLIED MUST BE A 11 ...'
      *                                  TO WS-ERROR-MSG   (line 1021-3)
      *        MOVE ZERO     TO CDEMO-ACCT-ID              (line 1024)
      *        GO TO 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT-EXIT                (line 1025)
      *    END-IF.
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC5 "STARTBR fails (EIBRESP
      *  =12 NOTOPEN)" along the input-error short-circuit branch.
      *  Production line 433 in 0000-MAIN guards 9000-READ-FORWARD
      *  with `IF NOT FLG-ACCTFILTER-NOT-OK AND NOT FLG-CARDFILTER
      *  -NOT-OK`; when 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT sets FLG-ACCTFILTER-NOT-
      *  OK at line 1019, the guard is FALSE and STARTBR is never
      *  issued -- the production invariant equivalent to the AAP
      *  TC5 STARTBR-failure path.
      *
      *  Input '0000000000A' is 11 chars (matches CC-ACCT-ID PIC
      *  X(11) so line-1007 OR SPACES is FALSE), alphanumeric
      *  (trailing 'A' fails IS NOT NUMERIC TRUE on line 1017),
      *  and the redefined CC-ACCT-ID-N PIC 9(11) view is not
      *  packed-decimal-zero so line-1009 EQUAL ZEROS is FALSE.
      *  Test-author supplied; NOT derived from production logic.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '1'         - WS-INPUT-FLAG flipped by line 1018 SET
      *                  INPUT-ERROR (88-level VALUE '1' per line 60).
      *    '0'         - WS-EDIT-ACCT-FLAG flipped by line 1019 SET
      *                  FLG-ACCTFILTER-NOT-OK (88-level VALUE '0'
      *                  per line 62).  KEY differential -- a non-
      *                  NOT-OK result here would break the line-
      *                  433 STARTBR-suppression invariant.
      *    'ACCOUNT FILTER,IF SUPPLIED MUST BE A 11 DIGIT NUMBER'
      *                - WS-ERROR-MSG literal MOVE'd verbatim by
      *                  production lines 1021-1023.  COMMA
      *                  IMMEDIATELY after "FILTER" preserved
      *                  exactly as in production source.
      *    '00000000000' - CDEMO-ACCT-ID flipped by line 1024 MOVE
      *                  ZERO (PIC 9(11) zero per COCOM01Y line 38).
      *                  cobol-check 0.2.16 EXPECT compares the field's
      *                  byte image as 11 ASCII '0' characters.
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES -- no-CICS invariant.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDLIC 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT rejects non-numeric acct'
            MOVE '0000000000A' TO CC-ACCT-ID
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT THRU 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-INPUT-FLAG TO BE '1'
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-ACCT-FLAG TO BE '0'
            EXPECT WS-ERROR-MSG TO BE
                'ACCOUNT FILTER,IF SUPPLIED MUST BE A 11 DIGIT NUMBER'
            EXPECT CDEMO-ACCT-ID TO BE '00000000000'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC6 -- YYYY-STORE-PFKEY maps DFHPF3 to CCARD-AID-PFK03
      *
      *  Drives YYYY-STORE-PFKEY (CSSTRPFY) along the PF3 exit arm:
      *
      *    WHEN EIBAID IS EQUAL TO DFHPF3                   (line 34)
      *      SET CCARD-AID-PFK03 TO TRUE                    (line 35)
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC6 "PF3 exits with ENDBR".
      *  The literal AAP TC6 requires driving 0000-MAIN's IF CCARD
      *  -AID-PFK03 AND CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM EQUAL LIT-THISPGM branch
      *  (lines 384-406) end-to-end through XCTL PROGRAM(LIT-MENU
      *  PGM) -- requires the CICS translator pass.  TC6 substitutes
      *  a direct PERFORM of YYYY-STORE-PFKEY with EIBAID=DFHPF3
      *  to validate the FIRST mapping in the dispatch chain that
      *  reaches the IF CCARD-AID-PFK03 guard.
      *
      *  Together with TC2 (DFHPF8 -> 'PFK08') and TC3 (DFHPF7 ->
      *  'PFK07'), TC6 covers the three operationally-significant
      *  PF arms -- exit (PF3), backward (PF7), forward (PF8).
      *  The production 0000-MAIN dispatch on lines 371-380 remaps
      *  any PFKey OTHER than ENTER / PF3 / PF7 / PF8 back to ENTER
      *  (lines 378-380), so the PF1/PF2/PF4-PF6/PF9-PF12 arms of
      *  YYYY-STORE-PFKEY are not operationally reachable for
      *  COCRDLIC -- testing only PF3/PF7/PF8 covers the surface.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'PFK03'    - CCARD-AID populated by SET CCARD-AID-PFK03
      *                 TO TRUE (CSSTRPFY line 35).  88-level VALUE
      *                 declared on CVCRD01Y line 11.
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES -- no-CICS invariant.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDLIC YYYY-STORE-PFKEY maps DFHPF3 to PFK03'
            MOVE DFHPF3 TO EIBAID
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM YYYY-STORE-PFKEY THRU YYYY-STORE-PFKEY-EXIT
            EXPECT CCARD-AID TO BE 'PFK03'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC7 -- 9500-FILTER-RECORDS excludes record on account mismatch
      *
      *  Drives 9500-FILTER-RECORDS (production lines 1382-1411)
      *  along the FLG-ACCTFILTER-ISVALID + non-matching-account
      *  EXCLUSION arm:
      *
      *    SET WS-DONOT-EXCLUDE-THIS-RECORD TO TRUE        (line 1383)
      *    IF FLG-ACCTFILTER-ISVALID                       (line 1385)
      *       IF  CARD-ACCT-ID = CC-ACCT-ID                (line 1386)
      *           CONTINUE                                 (line 1387)
      *       ELSE                                         (line 1388)
      *           SET WS-EXCLUDE-THIS-RECORD  TO TRUE      (line 1389)
      *           GO TO 9500-FILTER-RECORDS-EXIT           (line 1390)
      *       END-IF
      *    ...
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC7 "Filter by card number
      *  prefix": 9500-FILTER-RECORDS is the production paragraph
      *  that decides whether each READNEXT record (in 9000-READ-
      *  FORWARD line 1159 / 9100-READ-BACKWARDS line 1335) is
      *  admitted to the 7-row WS-SCREEN-DATA table or skipped.
      *  The implementation supports filtering by either CC-ACCT-
      *  ID (lines 1385-1394) or CC-CARD-NUM (lines 1396-1405);
      *  TC7 exercises the account-id arm (the more common upstream
      *  dispatch -- a non-admin user entering via COMEN01C carries
      *  CDEMO-ACCT-ID in the COMMAREA which becomes CC-ACCT-ID
      *  via 1300-SETUP-SCREEN-ATTRS).
      *
      *  Test sets FLG-ACCTFILTER-ISVALID TO TRUE so the outer guard
      *  is TRUE, then sets CC-ACCT-ID and CARD-ACCT-ID to DIFFERENT
      *  values so the IF on line 1386 is FALSE and the ELSE branch
      *  fires.  CARD-ACCT-ID is a CARD-RECORD field via COPY
      *  CVACT02Y; populated directly to drive the EXCLUSION arm.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '0'        - WS-FILTER-RECORD-FLAG flipped by line 1389
      *                 SET WS-EXCLUDE-THIS-RECORD (88-level VALUE
      *                 '0' per COCRDLIC.cbl line 148).  KEY
      *                 differential -- if line 1389 were inverted
      *                 (KEEP instead of EXCLUDE), this would fail.
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES -- no-CICS invariant.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDLIC 9500-FILTER-RECORDS excludes acct mismatch'
            MOVE '1'           TO WS-EDIT-ACCT-FLAG
            MOVE '00000000001' TO CC-ACCT-ID
            MOVE '00000000002' TO CARD-ACCT-ID
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 9500-FILTER-RECORDS THRU 9500-FILTER-RECORDS-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-FILTER-RECORD-FLAG TO BE '0'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC8 -- 9000-READ-FORWARD ENDFILE on first page (QA Issue 2)
      *
      *  Drives 9000-READ-FORWARD (production lines 1124-1262) along
      *  the WHEN DFHRESP(ENDFILE) branch (lines 1233-1245).  Off-
      *  platform GnuCOBOL comments out EXEC CICS STARTBR/READNEXT
      *  /ENDBR (precompiler substitutes CONTINUE), but the EVALUATE
      *  WS-RESP-CD remains live.  Pre-setting WS-RESP-CD = ENDFILE
      *  (DFHBMSCA value 20) drives the branch directly.  Setting
      *  WS-CA-SCREEN-NUM=1 plus the paragraph's own MOVE ZEROES TO
      *  WS-SCRN-COUNTER on line 1141 satisfies the line-1241/1242
      *  IF, setting WS-NO-RECORDS-FOUND TRUE -- the canonical
      *  empty-result-set diagnostic state.  Off-platform expression
      *  of QA Phase 3.2 ENDFILE EIBRESP=20 expectation.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    READ-LOOP-EXIT     - SET TRUE on production line 1234.
      *    CA-NEXT-PAGE-NOT-EXISTS - SET TRUE on line 1235.
      *    WS-NO-RECORDS-FOUND - SET TRUE on line 1244 because both
      *                         WS-CA-SCREEN-NUM=1 (test prelude)
      *                         AND WS-SCRN-COUNTER=0 (paragraph's
      *                         own MOVE ZEROES line 1141).  The SET
      *                         on an 88-level overwrites the prior
      *                         MOVE 'NO MORE RECORDS TO SHOW' (line
      *                         1239) with WS-NO-RECORDS-FOUND's
      *                         VALUE clause: 'NO RECORDS FOUND FOR
      *                         THIS SEARCH CONDITION.' (line 122).
      *                         WS-ERROR-MSG ends up holding that
      *                         value -- the canonical empty-result
      *                         diagnostic text.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDLIC 9000-READ-FORWARD ENDFILE first page'
            MOVE 20 TO WS-RESP-CD
            MOVE 1  TO WS-CA-SCREEN-NUM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 9000-READ-FORWARD THRU 9000-READ-FORWARD-EXIT
            EXPECT READ-LOOP-EXIT TO BE TRUE
            EXPECT CA-NEXT-PAGE-NOT-EXISTS TO BE TRUE
            EXPECT WS-NO-RECORDS-FOUND TO BE TRUE
            EXPECT WS-ERROR-MSG TO BE
                'NO RECORDS FOUND FOR THIS SEARCH CONDITION.'
            EXPECT WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC9 -- 9000-READ-FORWARD WHEN OTHER error path (QA Issue 2)
      *
      *  Drives 9000-READ-FORWARD along the WHEN OTHER branch (lines
      *  1246-1255) -- the CICS-error pathway covering NOTOPEN
      *  (DFHBMSCA=19), NOTFND (=13), and any other non-NORMAL/non-
      *  DUPREC/non-ENDFILE response.  Pre-setting WS-RESP-CD = 19
      *  (NOTOPEN; the value QA Phase 3.2 explicitly expected) drives
      *  the production error-flag flow:
      *
      *    SET READ-LOOP-EXIT             TO TRUE      (line 1249)
      *    MOVE 'READ'                    TO ERROR-OPNAME (1250)
      *    MOVE LIT-CARD-FILE='CARDDAT '  TO ERROR-FILE (1251)
      *    MOVE WS-FILE-ERROR-MESSAGE     TO WS-ERROR-MSG (1254)
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of QA Phase 3.2 STARTBR error
      *  EIBRESP=12 NOTOPEN expectation (QA used 12; production
      *  treats any non-{0,14,20} as WHEN OTHER -- 19 / NOTOPEN
      *  is functionally identical for branch-coverage purposes).
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    READ-LOOP-EXIT - SET TRUE line 1249 (88 VALUE '0').
      *    'READ'         - line 1250 literal MOVE to ERROR-OPNAME
      *                     (PIC X(8)); space-padded to 'READ    '.
      *    'CARDDAT '     - LIT-CARD-FILE PIC X(8) lines 213-214
      *                     MOVE'd to ERROR-FILE (PIC X(9)) line
      *                     1251 with one space pad: 'CARDDAT  '.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDLIC 9000-READ-FORWARD WHEN OTHER error path'
            MOVE 19 TO WS-RESP-CD
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 9000-READ-FORWARD THRU 9000-READ-FORWARD-EXIT
            EXPECT READ-LOOP-EXIT TO BE TRUE
            EXPECT ERROR-OPNAME TO BE 'READ    '
            EXPECT ERROR-FILE TO BE 'CARDDAT  '
            EXPECT WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC10 -- 9100-READ-BACKWARDS WHEN OTHER (initial) (QA Issue 2)
      *
      *  Drives 9100-READ-BACKWARDS (production lines 1265-1372) along
      *  the initial READPREV's WHEN OTHER branch (lines 1308-1318).
      *  This is the FIRST-FAULT exit path: the initial READPREV
      *  fails before entering the loop, so SET READ-LOOP-EXIT and
      *  GO TO 9100-READ-BACKWARDS-EXIT short-circuits to the ENDBR
      *  cleanup at line 1377.  Pre-setting WS-RESP-CD = 19 drives
      *  the GO TO 9100-READ-BACKWARDS-EXIT on line 1317.
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of QA Phase 3.2 backward-browse
      *  error-handling expectation; companion to TC9.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    READ-LOOP-EXIT - SET TRUE line 1311.
      *    'READ'         - line 1312 literal MOVE to ERROR-OPNAME.
      *    'CARDDAT '     - LIT-CARD-FILE MOVE'd to ERROR-FILE 1313.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDLIC 9100-READ-BACKWARDS WHEN OTHER initial'
            MOVE 19 TO WS-RESP-CD
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 9100-READ-BACKWARDS THRU 9100-READ-BACKWARDS-EXIT
            EXPECT READ-LOOP-EXIT TO BE TRUE
            EXPECT ERROR-OPNAME TO BE 'READ    '
            EXPECT ERROR-FILE TO BE 'CARDDAT  '
            EXPECT WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  End of testsuite COCRDLIC CARD LIST BROWSE TRANSACTION
      ******************************************************************
